# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# File context specifications for the lamadist local policy module
# (see lamadist.te).
#
# Intentionally empty after the W12 triage: none of the residual
# denials is fixed by a file-context entry here.  The natural
# candidate was the persisted ssh host keys at /var/lib/ssh (a
# sshd_key_t label would let refpolicy handle ssh_keygen_t/sshd_t
# access natively, replacing the var_lib_t allows in lamadist.te),
# but nothing relabels /var: /var/lib/ssh is created at runtime on
# the LUKS /var (var_lib_t from its parent) and lamadist-var-encrypt
# seeds /var with cp -a (label-preserving, no restorecon), so an fc
# entry here would never be applied.  Making it effective would need
# a restorecon of /var/lib/ssh, which lives in
# classes/lamadist-image.bbclass (outside this recipe's file set) --
# recorded for a later pass; the lamadist.te allows cover it for now.
#
# The /etc/ld.so.cache var_t mislabel that drove the denial storm is
# fixed at its source -- lamadist-image.bbclass masks ldconfig.service,
# so the cache is served correctly-labeled from the read-only lower --
# not by a build-time fc entry, so it does not belong here either.  The
# merged /etc root itself stays var_t (the overlay upperdir's type) and
# is deliberately not relabeled: base refpolicy lets every domain
# search a var_t dir, so it needs no fc entry.
